    "created_at": "2020-01-29T17:16:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-29T17:16:45Z",
    "body": "A better test here would probably be `x.getAttribute(\"codebase\")`. If it appears normalized then we know that the attribute is a USVString. I assume the URL parser does require a scalar value string, so going through the getter (which uses the URL parser) isn’t super instructive. And indeed in Chrome, `getAttribute` returns the original unpaired surrogate. (Haven’t tested other browsers.)",
